\docType{package}
\name{LFQPCA-package}
\alias{LFQPCA-package}
\alias{LFQPCA}
\title{Longitudinal functional quantile principal component analysis and regression}
\description{
Quantile decomposition of curves recorded at repeated visits into a population
surface, persistent subject trajectories and transient visit deviations, and
quantile regression of a scalar response on the two subject-level components.
The package also generates the data of the simulation designs of the
accompanying paper.
}
\details{
Subject \eqn{i} is seen at visits \eqn{j = 1, \ldots, J_i}{j = 1, ..., J_i} at
times \eqn{T_{ij}}{T_ij}. Each visit gives a curve \eqn{Y_{ij}(s)}{Y_ij(s)} on a
grid of the functional domain and, possibly, a scalar response
\eqn{V_{ij}}{V_ij}. With standardized time
\eqn{u_{ij} = (T_{ij} - \bar T)/s_T}{u_ij = (T_ij - mean(T))/sd(T)} and
\eqn{H(u) = (1, u, \ldots, u^p)^\top}{H(u) = (1, u, ..., u^p)'}, the conditional
\eqn{\tau}{tau}-quantile of the curves is modeled as
\deqn{Q_\tau\{Y_{ij}(s)\} = H(u_{ij})^\top \eta(s) + \xi_i^\top \{\phi_0(s) + u_{ij}\phi_1(s)\} + \zeta_{ij}^\top \psi(s).}{Q_tau(Y_ij(s)) = H(u_ij)' eta(s) + xi_i' (phi_0(s) + u_ij phi_1(s)) + zeta_ij' psi(s).}
The persistent component
\eqn{B_{ij}(s) = \xi_i^\top \{\phi_0(s) + u_{ij}\phi_1(s)\}}{B_ij(s) = xi_i' (phi_0(s) + u_ij phi_1(s))}
gives every subject its own functional intercept and slope in time, and the
transient component \eqn{U_{ij}(s) = \zeta_{ij}^\top \psi(s)}{U_ij(s) = zeta_ij' psi(s)}
holds the deviations of single visits. The visit scores of a subject are
orthogonal to its time design, \eqn{H_i^\top Z_i = 0}{H_i' Z_i = 0}, where the
rows of \eqn{H_i}{H_i} and \eqn{Z_i}{Z_i} are \eqn{H(u_{ij})^\top}{H(u_ij)'} and
\eqn{\zeta_{ij}^\top}{zeta_ij'}. Visit deviations thus carry no polynomial trend
within a subject and, with centered subject scores, \eqn{\eta}{eta} is the
average of the subjects' own trends.

\code{lfqpca} fits the model at one quantile level, and
\code{lfqpca_continuation} reaches other levels from the median in small steps.
The regression model
\deqn{Q_{\tau_R}(V_{ij}) = G(u_{ij})^\top \alpha + C_{ij}^\top \beta + \langle \gamma_B, B_{ij} \rangle + \langle \gamma_U, U_{ij} \rangle}{Q_tauR(V_ij) = G(u_ij)' alpha + C_ij' beta + <gamma_B, B_ij> + <gamma_U, U_ij>}
uses the components of an LFQPCA fit at level \eqn{\tau_F}{tau_F}; it is fitted
by \code{lfqpcr_from_lfqpca}, or together with the first stage by
\code{lfqpcr}. The dimensions and the level \eqn{\tau_F}{tau_F} can be chosen by
\code{lfqpca_cv} and \code{lfqpcr_cv}, and \code{lfqpcr_bootstrap} resamples
subjects.

The simulation designs are generated by \code{lfqpca_simulate} (Experiment I,
designs D1 to D7) and \code{lfqpcr_simulate} (Experiment II, Case1 to Case6).
}
